        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1453">

                <pb facs="1172" n="1056" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1056"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2064.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of
                        Nicaragua</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 5th instant by which you convey in courteous and
                    grateful terms, and by direction of your Government, the expression of its
                    sympathy on account of the killing of four and the wounding of six marines of
                    the United States in the discharge of their duty in Nicaragua, and inform me of
                    the honors that your Government has directed on the occasion of the funeral of
                    the men killed.</p>
                <p>I beg you, Mr. Minister, to be so good as to inform your Government of this
                    Government’s high appreciation of the friendly and sincere sentiments of your
                    note.</p>
                <p>While lamenting the circumstances of the death of these brave men, it is the hope
                    and expectation of the Government of the United States that they will not have
                    died in vain, but that from the sacrifice the people of Nicaragua will become
                    united in striving only for that which is for the best good of the country and
                    for the general happiness of the people.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
